21:45:56:617 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R101] CALIBRATOR mode=2 rung=0 site=data-scan | slots=57 data-slots=3 modules=174 gpa-calls=188 | resolved=1 creates=1 releases=0 live=1 sr-handle=known | latch: freed=0 reused=0 REFUSED=0 | evaluates=4368 captured=4368 | cost 2918 ns/frame | eval-copies=1768 eval-skips=0. R183: LIVE IS CREATES MINUS RELEASES and it is the field to read. A live count that climbs without bound means the title is not releasing what it recreates - a leak on the GAME's adapter, which is the same adapter our ring heap sits on. A live count that stays at one or two while creates climbs means recreation is matched and the pressure is somewhere else. A NEGATIVE live means we are missing creates rather than that releases exceeded them: some route resolved ReleaseFeature past our hooks, and the number is then a floor, not a count. R180: REFUSED is the one that must stay at zero. It counts scene features the latch set had no room for, and every one of them is a feature whose evaluates are skipped for the rest of the run. Four slots, freed on release since 0.2.5-dev; before that the set was append-only and a fifth create killed the velocity lane permanently. || THE GAME'S OWN TABLE: color=0x2066a65e1c0 depth=0x206efc6c7b0 MVEC=0x2066a76dc60 output=0x2066a76d2d0 | MVecScale 1485.0000,835.0000 | jitter 0.3057,-0.0625 | Reset=0 | CreateFlags=0xb -> DepthInverted=1 MVLowRes=1 MVJittered=0 IsHDR=1 AutoExposure=0 | quality=1 | NGX Width/Height 1485x835, OutWidth/OutHeight 2560x1440 | dynamic 1280x720..2560x1440 | subrect 1485x835 at color(0,0) depth(0,0) MV(0,0) out(0,0) | have=0x1fff. || HOW TO READ IT, REWRITTEN 2026-09-14 AFTER THIS LINE MISLED US FOR FOUR RUNS. evaluates=0 creates=0 DOES NOT MEAN THE HOOK FAILED. The first thing to check is whether the title has upscaling switched ON: with it off, the game never creates a DLSS feature, never evaluates, and a perfectly working hook reports exactly these zeros. creates=0 is the tell - an idle DLSS