21:46:02:658 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R63] DEPTH TRANSPORT f=8794 mode=1 (TRANSPORTED AND BOUND) | producer: valid=8796 invalid=0 size-rejected=0, arm held 0 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=5150 invalid=0 contract mismatches=0 | region 1485x835 fmt=41 pitch=6144 bytes=5130036 at slot offset 14746112 of 39970304. INVALID IS NOT AN ERROR: ReShade unbinds depth in menus and scene changes, and R61 established that shipping the zeros it leaves behind would hand the model a false flat plane. An invalid frame carries the colour and says so. WHAT WOULD BE AN ERROR is contract mismatches above zero, or valid staying at zero once you are in gameplay - that means the tap is not feeding us. 100.0% of sealed frames carried depth. | GPU 1: unpacked=5149 bound=4155 skipped=0, DepthInverted=1, flag disagreements=0 (the seal crossed the adapter and the slot flag did not, so any disagreement between them is real). BOUND vs SKIPPED IS THE R61 TEST: skipped counts frames where ReShade had no depth and the model was given NONE rather than the previous frame's - open a menu mid-stream and this must move.
21:46:02:659 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R315] f=8794 barrier route on the PUBLISHED source: fired 305 time(s) | copies own=4378 tap=0 | evaluate route not armed | value 2: phase=TAIL tail delivered=2610 judged=24 same=23. Fired > 0 with eval-copies flat = the game's own transition carries the vectors; fired = 0 = this engine's transition is not seen.
21:46:02:659 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=8794 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=4378 missing=4418 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 239 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=4376 invalid=774 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=6 | region 1485x835 fmt=10 pitch=12032 bytes=10046568 at slot offset 19876352 of 39970304 | GPU 1: unpacked=4375 bound=3760 skipped=395, scale=(1485.000, 835.000). 85.0% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
21:46:02:659 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=8794 | evaluates=4155 | elapsed 1=3162 2=625 3=25 4=23 5=8 6=8 7=8 8+=296 | worst=19 | 76.10% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
