21:46:19:943 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R63] DEPTH TRANSPORT f=9694 mode=1 (TRANSPORTED AND BOUND) | producer: valid=9697 invalid=0 size-rejected=0, arm held 0 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=6050 invalid=0 contract mismatches=0 | region 1485x835 fmt=41 pitch=6144 bytes=5130036 at slot offset 14746112 of 39970304. INVALID IS NOT AN ERROR: ReShade unbinds depth in menus and scene changes, and R61 established that shipping the zeros it leaves behind would hand the model a false flat plane. An invalid frame carries the colour and says so. WHAT WOULD BE AN ERROR is contract mismatches above zero, or valid staying at zero once you are in gameplay - that means the tap is not feeding us. 100.0% of sealed frames carried depth. | GPU 1: unpacked=6049 bound=4847 skipped=0, DepthInverted=1, flag disagreements=0 (the seal crossed the adapter and the slot flag did not, so any disagreement between them is real). BOUND vs SKIPPED IS THE R61 TEST: skipped counts frames where ReShade had no depth and the model was given NONE rather than the previous frame's - open a menu mid-stream and this must move.
