21:46:19:944 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=9694 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=5279 missing=4418 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 239 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=5276 invalid=774 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=6 | region 1485x835 fmt=10 pitch=12032 bytes=10046568 at slot offset 19876352 of 39970304 | GPU 1: unpacked=5275 bound=4452 skipped=395, scale=(1485.000, 835.000). 87.2% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
21:46:19:944 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=9694 | evaluates=4847 | elapsed 1=3646 2=833 3=25 4=23 5=8 6=8 7=8 8+=296 | worst=19 | 75.22% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
