21:47:05:697 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][SEAL] new f=12078 slot=5 gap=1 lat=51.66ms pitch=10240 fmt=28 bytes=14745600 bc=0(unimplemented) OK
21:47:05:701 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R101] CALIBRATOR mode=2 rung=0 site=data-scan | slots=57 data-slots=3 modules=174 gpa-calls=188 | resolved=1 creates=1 releases=0 live=1 sr-handle=known | latch: freed=0 reused=0 REFUSED=0 | evaluates=7968 captured=7968 | cost 4785 ns/frame | eval-copies=1768 eval-skips=0. R183: LIVE IS CREATES MINUS RELEASES and it is the field to read. A live count that climbs without bound means the title is not releasing what it recreates - a leak on the GAME's adapter, which is the same adapter our ring heap sits on. A live count that stays at one or two while creates climbs means recreation is matched and the pressure is somewhere else. A NEGATIVE live means we are missing creates rather than that releases exceeded them: some route resolved ReleaseFeature past our hooks, and the number is then a floor, not a count. R180: REFUSED is the one that must stay at zero. It counts scene features the latch set had no room for, and every one of them is a feature whose evaluates are skipped for the rest of the run. Four slots, freed on release since 0.2.5-dev; before that the set was append-only and a fifth create killed the velocity lane permanently. || THE GAME'S OWN TABLE: color=0x2066a65e1c0 depth=0x206efc6c7b0 MVEC=0x2066a76dc60 output=0x2066a76d2d0 | MVecScale 1485.0000,835.0000 | jitter -0.1348,-0.4878 | Reset=0 | CreateFlags=0xb -> DepthInverted=1 MVLowRes=1 MVJittered=0 IsHDR=1 AutoExposure=0 | quality=1 | NGX Width/Height 1485x835, OutWidth/OutHeight 2560x1440 | dynamic 1280x720..2560x1440 | subrect 1485x835 at color(0,0) depth(0,0) MV(0,0) out(0,0) | have=0x1fff. || HOW TO READ IT, REWRITTEN 2026-09-14 AFTER THIS LINE MISLED US FOR FOUR RUNS. evaluates=0 creates=0 DOES NOT MEAN THE HOOK FAILED. The first thing to check is whether the title has upscaling switched ON: with it off, the game never creates a DLSS feature, never evaluates, and a perfectly working hook reports exactly these zeros. creates=0 is the tell - an idle DLSS still creates its feature, an absent one does not. Only after confirming the setting is on
21:47:06:019 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R63] DEPTH TRANSPORT f=12094 mode=1 (TRANSPORTED AND BOUND) | producer: valid=12097 invalid=0 size-rejected=0, arm held 0 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=8450 invalid=0 contract mismatches=0 | region 1485x835 fmt=41 pitch=6144 bytes=5130036 at slot offset 14746112 of 39970304. INVALID IS NOT AN ERROR: ReShade unbinds depth in menus and scene changes, and R61 established that shipping the zeros it leaves behind would hand the model a false flat plane. An invalid frame carries the colour and says so. WHAT WOULD BE AN ERROR is contract mismatches above zero, or valid staying at zero once you are in gameplay - that means the tap is not feeding us. 100.0% of sealed frames carried depth. | GPU 1: unpacked=8449 bound=6685 skipped=0, DepthInverted=1, flag disagreements=0 (the seal crossed the adapter and the slot flag did not, so any disagreement between them is real). BOUND vs SKIPPED IS THE R61 TEST: skipped counts frames where ReShade had no depth and the model was given NONE rather than the previous frame's - open a menu mid-stream and this must move.
21:47:06:020 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R315] f=12094 barrier route on the PUBLISHED source: fired 305 time(s) | copies own=7679 tap=0 | evaluate route not armed | value 2: phase=TAIL tail delivered=5911 judged=24 same=23. Fired > 0 with eval-copies flat = the game's own transition carries the vectors; fired = 0 = this engine's transition is not seen.
21:47:06:020 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=12094 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=7679 missing=4418 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 239 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=7676 invalid=774 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=6 | region 1485x835 fmt=10 pitch=12032 bytes=10046568 at slot offset 19876352 of 39970304 | GPU 1: unpacked=7675 bound=6290 skipped=395, scale=(1485.000, 835.000). 90.8% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
21:47:06:020 [18072] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=12094 | evaluates=6685 | elapsed 1=4922 2=1395 3=25 4=23 5=8 6=8 7=8 8+=296 | worst=19 | 73.63% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
